# The comprehensive device-firmware baseline — flash once, then live on config [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

> **PLACEMENT RATIFIED, AUDIT COMPLETE.** It captures a comprehensive firmware-baseline design
> settled in conversation with David 2026-09-03 and was returned to the architect for an
> INDEPENDENT design-audit before landing — the same self-certification guard
> [CXC-BUSSTORE-CONVERSION-STATUS] applied to a code-conversion pass, and [SPEC:CXC-STORE] applied
> to a decision-conversion pass, applied here to a capability-bundle-conversion pass: the author of
> a bundle does not get to be its only reviewer. That audit flagged six provenance points and two
> ambiguous questions; David reviewed all eight in the 2026-09-03 session and RATIFIED all six
> corrections plus both clarifying answers (§0 and each touched node below, v0.2). Placement is now
> RATIFIED into `corpora/platform-specs/` ([CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-PLACEMENT]) — 93 remains the first
> free numeric prefix, chosen by listing this directory, not by counting.
>
> `lifecycle-position` says the same thing a query can read: **`ready-for-build — audit-complete,
> David-ratified 2026-09-03 (six provenance corrections + two clarifying answers applied), placement
> RATIFIED, not yet landed on hardware/code`**.
>
> **THE DRIVER, STATED PLAINLY.** USB-tethered reflash is the pain point. There is no OTA on any of
> this firmware today — none is planned in this baseline; OTA is the eventual real answer and is
> named only as the horizon (§7). So the bench session this baseline calls for buys EITHER a narrow
> fix that gets reflashed again next month, or a comprehensive one after which every device update is
> config-over-bus. Same labour at the bench, permanently different future: **flash once,
> comprehensively, then live on config.**

