## 0. The driver, its provenance, and placement

### [DEC-DEVICE-BASELINE-FLASH-ONCE-THEN-CONFIG] Bundle every confident firmware capability into ONE comprehensive flash pass; after it, all device updates are config-over-bus

- decision: every device visited for this baseline gets ALL SIX capabilities below in one USB session, not one capability at a time across six future bench visits. The alternative — landing each capability separately as it becomes confident — multiplies the exact cost this baseline exists to amortize: a USB-tethered visit to the physical device. Bundling is the point, not an optimization on top of it.
- provenance: architect-recommendation-david-agreed. The bundling strategy (flash once comprehensively) is the architect's framing of David's stated pain point (USB-tethered reflash) and David's explicit intent that OTA stay out of scope now; the six-capability set and their individual dispositions were settled with David in the 2026-09-03 session that this document converts.
- why-not-ota-instead: OTA is the mechanism that would make repeated USB visits unnecessary, and it is INTENTIONALLY not being built now (§7, [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-NONGOAL-OTA]) — so until it exists, minimizing the NUMBER of bench visits is the only lever available, and bundling is that lever.
- see-also: [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-NONGOAL-OTA]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

### [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-PLACEMENT] Placement is RATIFIED — stays in platform-specs/, same reasoning as [SPEC:CXC-STORE]'s ratified placement, 93 chosen by listing

- placement-status: RATIFIED (architect's call, 2026-09-03). This document stays filed in `corpora/platform-specs/`, alongside its dependencies and neighbours ([SPEC:CXC-STORE] at 92, [SPEC:CXC-REPOINT] at 74, [SPEC:CXC-ASSET-CHANGE-NOTIFY] at 80) — the SAME reasoning [CXC-STORE-PLACEMENT] gives for its own ratified placement: this is a spec carrying evidence slots, pre-/post-integration questions, and code-grounded capability dispositions, not merely a decision node, so it belongs beside the service/capability specs it depends on and extends rather than relocated toward the firmware source trees it specifies against (`cyd/`, `firmware/reactive_core/`).
- number-chosen: 93. The directory was listed (`ls corpora/platform-specs/`); 00-92 are taken (with the two known pre-existing filename-number collisions at 00 and 46, per [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT], neither touched by this addition) and 99 is a symlink to a `.smd` conventions file, not a `.lts` document — 93 is the first free `.lts` numeric prefix.
- ratification-resolved: whether this bundle belongs filed as a service/capability spec alongside [SPEC:CXC-STORE] and [SPEC:CXC-REPOINT], or should instead live closer to the firmware source trees it specifies against — RESOLVED above, by the architect: `platform-specs/`, for the reasons in `placement-status`.
- see-also: [CXC-VISION-PLACEMENT]
- see-also: [CXC-STORE-PLACEMENT]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

