## 2. Capability 2 — bus_binding endpoint-repoint: bench-unverified, already wired

### [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-BUS-BINDING] Repoint a device's bus master/storage URLs via retained state, no reflash — wired on both display mains, BENCH-UNVERIFIED

- capability: `cyd/src/bus_binding.h` / `.h`-declared accessors are ALREADY wired on both shared display mains — confirmed on read: `main.cpp` calls `bus_binding_boot_init` (line 1057), `bus_binding_control_init` (line 1186), and `bus_binding_tick` (line 1258, comment: "announce which bus + drive confirm echo"); `qualia_main.cpp` calls the same three (lines 499, 602, 741). A device is repointed by publishing a retained `_device/<id>/bus` (per-device) or `_device/broadcast/bus` (fleet-wide) binding carrying target URLs; the board ARMS a trial, reboots, resolves the new tier, and AUTO-REVERTS on failure within the confirm window. Precedence is per-device > global > COMPILED FLOOR — the compiled `COMPOSEIO_FW_DOCUMENT_STORE_URL:8420` (or whichever host is baked in) is now only the rescue floor, not the only address a board can ever reach.
- state-not-command: the binding is retained STATE the device reacts to, never a command sent to it — [DEC-BUS-BINDING-IS-STATE-NOT-A-COMMAND], the same discipline [DEC-ESP32-REMOTE-RESTART-BUS-COMMAND]'s `control-plane-legitimacy` property applies to restart.
- bench-unverified: `bus_binding.h`'s own header comment states it plainly — "THE REPOINT / CONFIRM / REVERT LOOP IS BENCH-UNVERIFIED. The state machine is host-proven, but a live binding repointing a real board + the auto-revert window is NOT bench-confirmed." [SPEC:CXC-REPOINT]'s `build-status` property independently confirms: BUILT + LANDED + host-verified across 83/83 (cyd) and 20/20 (reactive_core) SELFTESTS, all 8 envs compile — but the REMAINING GATE is explicitly named as "the BENCH FLASH (8 boards, no OTA, needs David + glass)." machine-green does not equal glass-green here.
- why-this-baseline-needs-it: without a live repoint, moving the fleet off `NODERED_HOST:8420` onto the merged store on `COMPOSEIO_MQTT_BROKER:8420` ([DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]) requires either a reflash per device or an interim reverse-proxy — [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]'s `fleet-repoint-decision` property names this exact fork and flags it as CXC-REPOINT territory, still open. This baseline's bench pass is the natural place to prove the repoint live, once, rather than as a separate future bench visit.
- provenance: DAVID-AGREED (retagged 2026-09-03, audit resolution). David explicitly confirmed the inclusion — he named bus_binding in his own agreement list in the 2026-09-03 session this document converts. The inclusion is CONFIRMED, not flagged; bus_binding was already built and wired for a different reason (the repoint spec [SPEC:CXC-REPOINT]) before this baseline was scoped, and the read that a comprehensive flash pass should prove it live rather than leave a second bench visit outstanding remains the architect's framing.
- depends-on: [SPEC:CXC-REPOINT]
- see-also: [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

