## 3. Capability 3 — content-hash on GET: bus_storage returns the hash it already computes

### [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-HASH-ON-GET] Return the content-hash on asset AND blob GET (ETag / X-Content-Hash) — the server already computes it for PUT, this stores and serves it

- capability: `services/bus_storage/change_notify.py`'s `content_hash()` (sha256, lowercase hex) is ALREADY computed server-side on every PUT, to drive `AssetChangeNotifier.notify()`'s `{old,new}` change event (confirmed on read: `content_hash = hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()`, called from `notify()` with both the prior and new bytes). It is computed and used TRANSIENTLY — for the change event — and is NOT currently persisted or served back on GET.
- what-changes: store the computed hash alongside the asset/blob at PUT time (a sidecar or index entry), and serve it on GET as a response header (`ETag` and/or `X-Content-Hash`) on both the asset route (`/api/v1/assets/*`) and the blob route (`/api/v1/blob/*`, the [SPEC:CXC-STORE] unified-store face).
- why-this-is-the-missing-link: this is what lets a device HOLD a hash for [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-ASSET-RELOAD]'s self-select rule WITHOUT computing it — the device fetches an asset at boot, reads the hash off the SAME response, and stores it as `held`. Without this, a device would need to either compute its own sha256 (explicitly ruled out, david-ruling: the device never computes sha256) or have no baseline hash to self-select against on first boot.
- provenance: architect-recommendation-david-agreed. The mechanism (store-at-PUT, serve-on-GET, reusing the hash the server already computes) is the architect's proposal; the underlying constraint it satisfies — the device never computes its own hash — is david-ruling.
- depends-on: [CXC-ASSET-CHANGE-NOTIFY]
- see-also: [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-ASSET-RELOAD]
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

---

## 4. Capability 4 — blob-route change-notify emit: extend the notifier past the asset tree

### [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-BLOB-NOTIFY] Extend `_notify_asset_change` to `/api/v1/blob` so migrated document_store docs emit change events like assets

- capability: `services/bus_storage/server.py`'s `_handle_config_put` marks the gap explicitly in its own comment (confirmed on read, `server.py` ~line 468 region): "SEAM, not a gap: [CXC-ASSET-CHANGE-NOTIFY] P-a is scoped to the asset tree only ([CXC-ACN-PRECEDENT] — unifying this route's own config-push notifier into asset-change-notify is a marked FUTURE follow-on, 'not yet unified in code'). Do not hang `_notify_asset_change` off this route." The `/api/v1/blob` route family — the [SPEC:CXC-STORE] unified-store face that now serves migrated `document_store` docs as `bus://<collection>/<id>.json` blobs — does not currently emit `{old,new}` change events on PUT the way `/api/v1/assets/*` does.
- what-changes: wire the SAME `AssetChangeNotifier.notify()` call the asset PUT handler already uses onto `_handle_blob_put`, so a migrated document (an app surface, a board_profile, a recipe — anything now living as a `bus://` blob per [SPEC:CXC-STORE]'s `[CXC-STORE-CAP-GET]` / `[CXC-STORE-CAP-LIST]` disposition) gets the same change-notify coverage an asset gets.
- ratified-by: David agreed to this extension explicitly in the 2026-09-03 session this document converts — a two-word "Yes, agreed" in response to the architect's proposal.
- provenance: ARCHITECT-RECOMMENDATION-DAVID-AGREED (retagged 2026-09-03, audit resolution) for the extension itself — architect-proposed, David agreed with "Yes, agreed"; architect-recommendation for the mechanism (reuse the existing notifier by reference rather than build a second one).
- see-also: [CXC-ASSET-CHANGE-NOTIFY]
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

