## 5. Capability 5 — doc:// purge: the per-device pass eliminates every remaining reference

### [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-DOC-PURGE] Purge doc:// wherever it exists — the fleet exits the cutover with doc:// genuinely gone, not merely deprecated

- capability: [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]'s `doc-scheme-ruling` property already records David's ruling: "doc:// FULLY deprecated — remove the `resolve.py`/`assets.py` compat alias, NO cross-ref rewrite; the 2 app-surface breaks (fleet-540-soak, minnow-bringup) surface and are fixed at source." The alias code itself is already removed (commit `0f2e07d`, confirmed by [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]'s `doc-scheme-ruling` and cutover-status properties). This capability is the DEVICE-FACING completion of that ruling: the per-device firmware/config pass this baseline performs is the moment to also eliminate any `doc://` reference reachable from device-served config, not just the two known app-surface refs.
- known-surface: the 2 known app-surface references — `apps/fleet-540-soak` and `apps/minnow-bringup` — per [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]'s ruling, fixed at source.
- unknown-surface: this baseline additionally requires checking on-device configs and any live-store docs reachable from the fleet for a `doc://` reference that predates the migration — an EMPTY census slot (§9), not a claim that none exist.
- distinction-from-cxc-store: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]'s `[CXC-STORE-CUTOVER-XREF-REWRITE]` names the cross-reference rewrite as OPTIONAL because the read-time compat alias would have covered it — but that alias is now REMOVED per David's fuller ruling here, which supersedes the optionality: with no alias, an un-rewritten `doc://` reference is a hard break, not a degraded-but-working path. This node records that supersession explicitly so the two documents are not read as contradicting each other.
- provenance: david-ruling (the FULL deprecation, no alias, no rewrite — [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]'s `doc-scheme-ruling`); architect-recommendation-david-agreed (folding the device-facing completion of the purge into this baseline's per-device pass, so it is not a separate future visit).
- see-also: [SPEC:CXC-STORE]
- see-also: [DEC-STORAGE-MERGED-DATA-ON-(a private host name, not published)-2026-09-02]
- part-of: [SPEC:CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE]

