**Version**: 0.2 — 2026-09-03, design-audit resolutions applied by factlattice-editor after David
ratified all six flagged provenance points plus two clarifying answers in the 2026-09-03 session.
Six provenance retags: (1) [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-BUS-BINDING] architect-inference -> DAVID-AGREED
(David named bus_binding in his own agreement list; inclusion CONFIRMED, no longer flagged); (2)
[CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-ASSET-RELOAD] restart-as-recovery-floor architect-recommendation ->
DAVID-RULING (David's original idea, his genesis turn: "the recovery mechanism is a restart"); (3)
[CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAPABILITY-THRESHOLD] reframed as a CAPABILITY PREDICATE evaluable from
`board_profile` (David: the gate is "does the device have sufficient RAM and compute," not "is it an
ESP32") — ESP32/RP2040 are examples that clear it, the CH32V003 an example that fails it, exclusion
DAVID-AGREED on the capability basis, not chip-family; (4) [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-BLOB-NOTIFY]
david-ruling -> ARCHITECT-RECOMMENDATION-DAVID-AGREED (architect-proposed, David's "Yes, agreed");
(5) [DD-DEVICE-BASELINE-DEFER-FETCH-BY-HASH] provenance split — deferral DAVID-RULING, trigger
conditions ARCHITECT-RECOMMENDATION — and the deferral is now recorded as CLOSING [CXC-ACN-RECOVERY]'s
usefulness-in-parallel question, per David's 2026-09-03 confirmation; (6)
[CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-TRANSPORT-SELECT-RUNTIME] provenance split — the outcome (no reflash to change
role, mode/UART pins config-selectable) DAVID-RULING, the mechanism (extend bus_transport_select)
ARCHITECT-RECOMMENDATION. Two clarifying answers applied: Q1 —
[CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-CAP-ASSET-RELOAD]'s `auto-recovery` property corrected from an assumed
BROKER-SIDE MQTT-retention mechanism to David's stated PRIMARY mechanism, DEVICE-SIDE inbound-message
buffering, recorded as an EMPTY capability to verify/build
([CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-PRE-DEVICE-SIDE-BUFFERING], [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-EV-10]), not an
already-present claim, with restart remaining the recovery floor beneath it; Q2 — resolved by
correction (5) above, closing [CXC-ACN-RECOVERY]. Every code-grounded claim (line numbers, function
names, file paths, header comments) from v0.1 is carried forward unchanged; nothing in that
grounding was touched by this audit pass. The one discrepancy left open by that pass —
[CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-SCOPE-PRECONDITION]'s claim that `dd7e049` ended the CAN-layout divergence,
contradicted by two corpus records that postdated the commit without recording its resolution — is
CLOSED as of 2026-09-03: `python/composeio/transport_can.py`, `services/can_mqtt_bridge/bridge.py`
and `cyd/src/bus_can_id.h` were read directly and all three implement `prio(3)|type(4)|ns_id(16)
|src(4)|scope(2)` identically, with `bridge.py` importing the codec functions from
`transport_can.py` rather than reimplementing them. [CXC-DEVICE-BASELINE-PRE-SCOPE-WIRE-VERIFY] is
now VERIFIED/MET (§9), [CXC-VISION-SCOPE-MEMBRANE] and [DEC-CAN-ARBITRATION-ID-LAYOUT-DIVERGENCE]
have been synced to match, and the scope-on-wire precondition for the relay/mothercard build is MET.
**Status**: Ratified — placement RATIFIED, audit-complete, David-ratified 2026-09-03. Ready for
build; every capability's own evidence slot (§10) remains EMPTY until the bench pass runs.
